    "result": "No leftover debug statements. Both fixes are in place and verified:\n\n**1. `frai setup --key/--global` bypassing the prompt** \u2014 root cause was Commander parsing `--key`/`--global` at the root program level (since it also declares those flags) before dispatching to the `setup`/`generate` subcommands, leaving the subcommand's own options empty. Fixed with `.enablePositionalOptions()` on the root program (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`), rebuilt to `dist/index.js`. Verified: `setup --key`, `setup --key --global`, `generate --key --global`, and the legacy root `--setup --key [--global]` all now work non-interactively.\n\n**2/3. Key-store rewrite and unreliable detection** \u2014 rewrote `packages/frai-core/src/config/key-store.js`:\n- `.env` reads/writes now parse line-by-line, skipping commented-out lines, matching optional `export`, quoted/unquoted values with trailing `# comment`, and taking the last definition when duplicated.\n- `setLocalApiKey` updates the matched line in place (preserving `export`) or appends a new line, leaving every other line byte-for-byte untouched.\n- `setGlobalApiKey` merges into existing JSON (preserving other fields) instead of overwriting, and throws without touching the file if the existing JSON is invalid.\n- `hasLocalApiKey`/`hasGlobalApiKey` now require a non-empty key rather than just file existence.\n- Function names/args/returns and file permissions (`0o600`/`0o700`) are unchanged.\n\nAdded 6 new tests to `key-store.test.js` covering these behaviors \u2014 all pass. `pnpm test` in `frai-core` still shows the same two pre-existing unrelated failures (`governance.test.js`, `eval/index.test.js`), nothing new broken.\n\nNote: I created a scratch `.sandbox/` directory at the repo root for manual CLI testing; deleting it was blocked by the sandbox's destructive-op guard, so it's still there if you want to remove it yourself (`rm -rf .sandbox`) \u2014 it's untracked and not part of the fix.",
